{"text": "Falling water makes about fourteen percent of the world's electricity. So how does a wall of water turn into power? Behind the dam, a lake holds a huge amount of water, high above the river below. That height is stored energy, and the taller the dam, the more energy every drop carries. A gate opens, and the water rushes down a giant pipe called the penstock, picking up speed as it falls. At the bottom, it slams into the blades of a turbine, and forces it to spin. The turbine's shaft turns the generator, where huge magnets spin past coils of copper wire. Moving magnets push the electrons in the copper along. That flow is electricity! A transformer then raises the voltage, so the power can travel hundreds of miles through power lines. Worldwide, hydropower made about forty-five hundred terawatt-hours in 2024, and the water simply carries on down the river. Water falls, a turbine spins, magnets move, and your lights turn on!", "voiceId": "Ddh3PpD0pGS5vi20kePJ", "modelId": "eleven_multilingual_v2", "speed": 1.15, "characters": ["F", "a", "l", "l", "i", "n", "g", " ", "w", "a", "t", "e", "r", " ", "m", "a", "k", "e", "s", " ", "a", "b", "o", "u", "t", " ", "f", "o", "u", "r", "t", "e", "e", "n", " ", "p", "e", "r", "c", "e", "n", "t", " ", "o", "f", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "w", "o", "r", "l", "d", "'", "s", " ", "e", "l", "e", "c", "t", "r", "i", "c", "i", "t", "y", ".", " ", "S", "o", " ", "h", "o", "w", " ", "d", "o", "e", "s", " ", "a", " ", "w", "a", "l", "l", " ", "o", "f", " ", "w", "a", "t", "e", "r", " ", "t", "u", "r", "n", " ", "i", "n", "t", "o", " ", "p", "o", "w", "e", "r", "?", " ", "B", "e", "h", "i", "n", "d", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "d", "a", "m", ",", " ", "a", " ", "l", "a", "k", "e", " ", "h", "o", "l", "d", "s", " ", "a", " ", "h", "u", "g", "e", " ", "a", "m", "o", "u", "n", "t", " ", "o", "f", " ", "w", "a", "t", "e", "r", ",", " ", "h", "i", "g", "h", " ", "a", "b", "o", "v", "e", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "r", "i", "v", "e", "r", " ", 